WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.002
-As you guys know, we're always
striving to get better

00:00:03.002 --> 00:00:04.470
here at "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:09.375
♪ Harder, better,
faster, stronger ♪

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:10.810
Which is why we asked
viewers at home

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:12.445
to send in
any suggestions that they have

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.680
just to get some feedback about
what you guys think of the show,

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.750
things you'd like to see us do,
that kind of stuff.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.652
So tonight, let's look inside
the audience suggestion box.

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:24.757
-♪ Look into the box,
the suggestion box ♪

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:29.529
-Here we go here. This first one
is from Owen Sheckart.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:31.564
"Hey, Jimmy, I like watching
'The Bachelor,'

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:34.233
but some parts of it
are too emotional for me.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:35.634
You should fix that."

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:38.137
Well, we always take
our suggestions seriously here.

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:41.373
So here's an emotionally intense
scene from "The Bachelor"

00:00:41.373 --> 00:00:44.677
re-voiced with the least
emotional person we know, Siri.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:47.013
Take a look.

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:48.881 line:0%
-I'm sorry that
I hurt your feelings.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:51.317 line:0%
Thank you.
I accept your apology,

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:54.787 line:0%
but I think that we have
very different realities

00:00:54.787 --> 00:00:57.289 line:0%
of what occurred.
Regardless of what happened --

00:00:57.289 --> 00:00:59.592 line:0%
Well, if it didn't happen,
why are you apologizing?

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:00.726 line:0%
Matt had mentioned

00:01:00.726 --> 00:01:02.862 line:0%
that you think I'm toxic
and manipulative.

00:01:02.862 --> 00:01:04.530 line:0%
I do think you're those things.

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.032 line:0%
I don't want
to continue fighting.

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:07.533 line:0%
I'm not trying to fight, either,

00:01:07.533 --> 00:01:10.937 line:0%
but I think that, like,
we are like oil and vinegar.

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:12.772
-Wow. [ Laughs ]

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:15.174
[ Applause ]

00:01:15.174 --> 00:01:17.443
I'd watch a whole episode
of that, man. I like that.

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:18.877
Let's get to another
suggestion here.

00:01:18.877 --> 00:01:20.846
This is from Liza Geller.

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:23.582
"Hey, Jimmy. You're always
asking guests questions.

00:01:23.582 --> 00:01:26.352
You should try asking the camera
a question."

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.221
Try asking
the camera a question?

00:01:29.221 --> 00:01:31.624
That's a great idea.
I guess I can give it a shot.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:35.861
Okay, Camera, do you work
at "The Tonight Show"?

00:01:35.861 --> 00:01:37.297
Oh.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:41.533
Do you like working at the show?

00:01:41.533 --> 00:01:45.572
Can you tell us your favorite
person in the studio?

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.173
Come on, Camera.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.974
Show us your favorite person
in the studio.

00:01:48.974 --> 00:01:51.511
We all want to know.

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:52.845
Tha--

00:01:52.845 --> 00:01:55.348
Wait, what?

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:57.317
Wait, what --

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.285
What the hell?
-Come on!

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.586
-What the --
-Do this!

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:03.522
-Who let this guy in here?

00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:05.625
-Eat [bleep] [bleep]

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:07.193
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:08.561
[ Applause ]

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:11.964
That guy's a menace.
That guy's a menace right there.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.467
-Nice [bleep] studio!

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:16.201
[Bleep] hole!

00:02:16.201 --> 00:02:18.972
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:39.525
At least he's wearing a mask.

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:42.962
Alright. This next one here
is from Michelle Pirozi.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.631
"Hey, Jimmy. I love
'Bridgerton.'"

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:47.400
Me, too.
"It has such a good theme song,

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.402
but I wish it had lyrics.
Could you add some?"

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:51.804
That's a great idea.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:54.073
Tariq, Quest, you guys
want to take this one?

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:55.842
-You got it.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:58.110
-Sure.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.579
[ "Bridgerton"
theme song playing ]

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:05.985
-♪ Old timey people
with cool sideburns ♪

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.288
-♪ Who like to dance ♪

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:14.727
-♪ Old timey people
wearing wigs ♪

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:17.129
-♪ And fancy pants ♪

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:21.034
-♪ They're riding horses now ♪

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:25.838
-♪ And drinking tea ♪

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:30.777
-♪ They're also
eating crumpets ♪

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:34.380
-♪ Everyone is British ♪

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:40.753
-♪ Old timey people
with cool sideburns ♪

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:44.757
-♪ And fancy pants ♪

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.093
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:53.199
-Neither of you have ever seen
the show, have you?

00:03:53.199 --> 00:03:54.968
-Not at all.

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.836
-Nay.

00:04:00.472 --> 00:04:03.342
-Let's get another
suggestion here.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:06.212
Oh, this one is from
Vivian Zelter.

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:08.848
"Hey, Jimmy, you should
advertise more products

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:10.717
on the show."

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:13.686
That's an interesting suggestion
but it just doesn't feel right

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.621
to do an ad
in the middle of the show.

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:19.191
I mean, just thinking about it
leaves a bad taste in my mouth,

00:04:19.191 --> 00:04:22.895
unlike...Paul Leonard's
Edible Calculators,

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:26.199
the first nonfunctional,
fully digestible calculators.

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:30.536
I just crunched the numbers,
and...they're delicious.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:32.605
Now with even less mercury!

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:36.042
♪♪

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:38.378
[ Applause ]

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:40.513
Okay. We're down to
our last suggestion here.

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:43.115
It is from Matt Gilberg.
"Hey, Jimmy.

00:04:43.115 --> 00:04:45.484
I know there are a lot of shows
that film in New York City.

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:49.054
So I was wondering, do you ever
visit any of the other shows?"

00:04:49.054 --> 00:04:51.924
Well, it's funny you ask that,
because I do.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:56.129
It's all thanks to my TV portal.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:58.798
Yeah.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.433
The TV portal can put me...

00:05:01.433 --> 00:05:04.403
[ Whoosh ]

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:06.639
...in any other New York show.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.074
Let me show you.

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:12.611
-We have a great show
for you guys.

00:05:12.611 --> 00:05:14.079
I'm really excited!

00:05:14.079 --> 00:05:16.782
Oh! Jimmy. You okay?

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:17.950
-[ Weakly ] Hi, Drew.
-Okay.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.051
-Oh, God.

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:20.853
-Well, that's
all the time we have

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:22.922
for "Audience Suggestion Box."

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:24.289
Stick around, everyone,

00:05:24.289 --> 00:05:27.560
and we'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show."

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.462 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:33.566 line:0%
♪♪

